    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/48064": {
      "title": "Psychology-Student Assistant",
      "description": "Psychology-Student Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Psychology-Student Assistant Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $15.00 Hourly Position Type Student Apply Description Purpose of this Position: To support the psychology department with educating and supporting students as well as to support faculty research and scholarship. Tasks could be focused around different roles depending upon faculty and department needs. Essential Job Functions (include, but are not limited to) : Supporting departmental efforts in advising, career opportunities, communication, enrollment management activities, student clubs and organizations, advisory mechanisms, etc. • Supporting faculty in course preparation – copying materials, setting up activities, etc. Supporting faculty course implementation and student tracking Assisting faculty with research, data collection, literature reviews, lab tasks, etc. • Tutoring students as needed in specific courses in need of tutoring support Qualifications Requirements: Must be a currently enrolled undergraduate student at Western New England University, preferably a psychology major (or something similar) with affiliated knowledge. Required Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Ability to take initiative and work on projects consistently Clear communication skills – with supervisor/faculty, oral and written Dependability – commitment to follow-through Showing up and working when planned - Flexibility to complete the work as needed by faculty when tasks may change regularly Office 365 skills and familiarity with word, excel, PowerPoint, and Canva at a minimum Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/135857": {
      "title": "Enrollment Services-Student Assistant",
      "description": "Enrollment Services-Student Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Enrollment Services-Student Assistant Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $15.00 Hourly Position Type Student Apply Description To provide clerical assistance to the Directors, Specialists, Student Services Administrators, and Receptionists of SAS with a minimum of supervision. Distinguishing Characteristics: Act as clerical support. DESCRIPTION OF DUTIES AND TASKS : Essential Job Functions : · File · Assist with mailings to students and faculty · Basic data entry · Inter-office errands · Other duties as assigned by the Directors, Specialists, Student Services Administrators, and Receptionists Marginal Job Functions : · Operate office machinery Qualifications Ability to file and retrieve data from student files. Good interpersonal skills and the capacity to follow directions. Capacity to adhere strictly to standards of preserving confidentiality of information. Skill in the use of computer systems Good organizational skills Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/135625": {
      "title": "Pharmacy Practice - Student Assistant",
      "description": "Pharmacy Practice - Student Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Pharmacy Practice - Student Assistant Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $15.00 Hourly Position Type Student Apply Description The Department of Pharmacy Practice is seeking a student worker to assist faculty with preparation and organization of pharmacy laboratory activities.  PharmD students are encouraged to apply. Responsibilities Assist with preparation of materials for pharmacy laboratory activities Prepare mock prescriptions and other instructional materials using faculty-provided information Gather and organize supplies for upcoming laboratory sessions Assist with laboratory inventory organization Restock and organize instructional materials and supplies Assist with setup and breakdown of laboratory activities Complete other laboratory preparation tasks as assigned by faculty Qualifications Qualifications Current WNE student in good academic standing Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Dependable and able to follow written and verbal instructions Ability to work independently Familiarity with pharmacy laboratory activities preferred PharmD students are encouraged to apply. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/135616": {
      "title": "Pharmacy Practice - Student Assistant",
      "description": "Pharmacy Practice - Student Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Pharmacy Practice - Student Assistant Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $15.00 Hourly Position Type Student Apply Description The Department of Pharmacy Practice is seeking a WNE student to assist faculty with preparation and coordination of Objective Structured Clinical Examinations (OSCEs) and standardized patient activities. Because this position may involve access to confidential assessment materials, applicants cannot be currently enrolled in the PharmD program. Responsibilities Assist with preparation and organization of OSCE materials Assist with preparation of standardized patient training materials Help coordinate communications and materials for standardized patients Review standardized patient instructions for clarity and consistency Organize case materials and supporting documents Assist with scheduling and other administrative aspects of standardized patient activities Assist with in-person or virtual standardized patient training as needed Maintain strict confidentiality of all OSCE cases and assessment materials Complete other OSCE-related preparation tasks as assigned Qualifications Must not be enrolled in the PharmD program or pre-pharmacy Current WNE student in good academic standing Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Strong written and verbal communication skills Dependable and able to work independently Comfortable using Microsoft Office/365 and Zoom Able to maintain strict confidentiality regarding assessment materials Students in health sciences, psychology, biology, neuroscience, education, communication, or other related programs are encouraged to apply. Confidentiality This position may involve access to secure educational assessment materials. The student worker must maintain strict confidentiality and may not share, reproduce, retain, photograph, or discuss OSCE cases or related assessment materials outside of assigned work. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/135611": {
      "title": "Pharmacy Practice - Student Assistant",
      "description": "Pharmacy Practice - Student Assistant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Pharmacy Practice - Student Assistant Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $15.00 - $15.00 Hourly Position Type Student Education Level None Apply Description Assist with marketing and promotion of continuing education programs Prepare and organize program materials Assist with attendee registration and communication Help maintain CE program documentation and records Provide administrative support before and following CE events Assist with other CE-related tasks as needed Qualifications Current WNE student in good academic standing Strong organizational and communication skills Attention to detail Comfortable using email and Microsoft Office/365 Ability to complete assignments independently and meet deadlines Students from any WNE program are encouraged to apply. Interest in event planning, marketing, communications, healthcare, or professional education is a plus. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/3C67A483237F6A324625AB95D568B0C1/jobs/132919": {
      "title": "Senior Director of Development/Director of Development",
      "description": "Senior Director of Development/Director of Development You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Senior Director of Development/Director of Development Springfield, MA 01119 Apply Overview Salary Range $115,000.00 - $145,000.00 Salary/year Position Type Full Time Staff Education Level Bachelor's Degree Apply Description Western New England University is accepting applications for the position of Senior Director of Development/Director of Development. The position level offered to the selected candidate will be based on experience. The hiring range for this position is: Director of Development (3-5 years of experience) - $100,000 - $125,000 Senior Director of Development (5+ years of experience) - $125,000 - $145,000 PURPOSE OF THIS POSITION : The Senior Development Director/Development Director is responsible for leading all development activities within three colleges or operational units (COU) of the University in effort to raise funding in support of the mission. In coordination with the Vice President for Advancement and other members of the Advancement Team, the position develops, implements and monitors a comprehensive fundraising plan to expand philanthropic support of the organization including strengthening relationships with key donors, identifying and cultivating new prospective donors, engaging with leadership of the CAU to build a strong culture of philanthropy, and working with the members of the Advancement Team to deliver programming that increases engagement and philanthropy. DISTINGUISHING CHARACTERISTICS: This position works closely with the Vice President for Advancement and serves on the senior management team for the Advancement Division. The position requires a collaborative and creative approach to redefining and solving problems, along with identifying alternate strategies that are novel and effective. Responsibilities include: Playing a key leadership role in the University’s fundraising activities, including providing strategic direction based on an analytical review of friend-and-fundraising data and donor behaviors, with special attention paid to creating and implementing strategies that focus on building a robust donor pipeline. Creating and implementing programs to build stronger relationships with alumni, parents, business leaders, faculty, and staff. Cultivating, soliciting, and stewarding of prospects and donors with the capacity to make gifts at all levels. Building strong relationships with colleagues across the University to achieve fundraising objectives. Qualifications QUALIFICATION STANDARDS: Seven years of fundraising experience Some management/supervisory experience Experience securing major gifts by strategically managing a portfolio and fostering meaningful relationships Highly developed leadership and organizational skills. A track record of working closely with senior leaders and providing the support necessary to ensure their success in development activities Proven ability to develop guidelines and metrics to track effectiveness of projects and processes Interpersonal skills to establish and maintain good working relationships ranging from senior management to technical and administrative staff Commitment to ethical practices in fundraising Demonstrated ability to manage conflict. Bachelor’s degree required. ERGONOMIC REQUIREMENTS: Sitting, standing, bending, walking, climbing stairs, and reaching as expected in normal office setting. Occasional lifting, not to exceed 25 pounds Western New England University is committed to enhancing diversity, equity, inclusion and belonging by acknowledging and embracing diversity of thought, opinion, and approach with colleagues regardless of background, culture, and organizational level.  WNE encourages diversity in our job applicants to ensure the best culture and work outcomes. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
